{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And they covered the eye of all the land, and the land darkened.</b> This teaches that they left no place empty, in the manner of what is written (Joel 2:9): ״בעיר ישקו בחומה ירוצון בבתים יעלו בעד החלונות יבאו כגנב״. And the word עין is from the sense of גוון (hue), for all the land changed from its hue to blackness."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The play on עין / גוון rests on a phonetic-semantic association between 'eye' and 'hue/color'; the linkage is literal in the Hebrew and cannot be smoothed without losing the point."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:32.742241562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}